	</Define>
	<!-- Automated production (written by Claude): what a city of yours builds when you let the governor choose its
		production (the city screen's "automate production" button). It builds the first building of this list that it
		can build, and nothing else: no units, no wonders, no buildings that aren't on the list. When nothing on the list
		can be built, the automation turns itself off and the city asks you what to build. Building classes from
		Buildings/CIV4BuildingClassInfos.xml (a civilization's unique building takes the place of its class), separated
		by commas or spaces; empty = K-Mod's governor chooses.
		A power plant is skipped where the city already has clean power, and a dirty one (Coal Plant, Shale Plant) also
		where it has any power, so HYDRO_PLANT, COAL_PLANT means a hydro plant if possible, else a coal plant.
		Left out so that they are never built: the cathedrals (Stupa, Cathedral, Academy, Mandir, Mosque, Synagogue,
		Pagoda) and the Nuclear Plant. -->
	<Define>
		<DefineName>AUTOMATED_PRODUCTION_ORDER</DefineName>
		<DefineTextVal>
			BUILDINGCLASS_COURTHOUSE, BUILDINGCLASS_GRANARY, BUILDINGCLASS_FORGE, BUILDINGCLASS_FACTORY,
			BUILDINGCLASS_HYDRO_PLANT, BUILDINGCLASS_COAL_PLANT,
			BUILDINGCLASS_LEVEE, BUILDINGCLASS_INDUSTRIAL_PARK, BUILDINGCLASS_LIGHTHOUSE, BUILDINGCLASS_AIRPORT,
			BUILDINGCLASS_HARBOR, BUILDINGCLASS_GROCER, BUILDINGCLASS_SUPERMARKET, BUILDINGCLASS_AQUEDUCT,
			BUILDINGCLASS_HOSPITAL, BUILDINGCLASS_PUBLIC_TRANSPORTATION, BUILDINGCLASS_RECYCLING_CENTER, BUILDINGCLASS_JAIL,
			BUILDINGCLASS_BUDDHIST_TEMPLE, BUILDINGCLASS_CHRISTIAN_TEMPLE, BUILDINGCLASS_CONFUCIAN_TEMPLE,
			BUILDINGCLASS_HINDU_TEMPLE, BUILDINGCLASS_ISLAMIC_TEMPLE, BUILDINGCLASS_JEWISH_TEMPLE, BUILDINGCLASS_TAOIST_TEMPLE,
			BUILDINGCLASS_COLOSSEUM, BUILDINGCLASS_BROADCAST_TOWER, BUILDINGCLASS_MARKET, BUILDINGCLASS_THEATRE,
			BUILDINGCLASS_BANK, BUILDINGCLASS_LIBRARY,
			BUILDINGCLASS_BUDDHIST_MONASTERY, BUILDINGCLASS_CHRISTIAN_MONASTERY, BUILDINGCLASS_CONFUCIAN_MONASTERY,
			BUILDINGCLASS_HINDU_MONASTERY, BUILDINGCLASS_ISLAMIC_MONASTERY, BUILDINGCLASS_JEWISH_MONASTERY,
			BUILDINGCLASS_TAOIST_MONASTERY,
			BUILDINGCLASS_UNIVERSITY, BUILDINGCLASS_OBSERVATORY, BUILDINGCLASS_LABORATORY, BUILDINGCLASS_INTELLIGENCE_AGENCY,
			BUILDINGCLASS_NATIONAL_SECURITY, BUILDINGCLASS_CUSTOM_HOUSE, BUILDINGCLASS_DRYDOCK, BUILDINGCLASS_BARRACKS,
			BUILDINGCLASS_BUNKER, BUILDINGCLASS_BOMB_SHELTER
		</DefineTextVal>
	</Define>
	<!-- Game setup (written by Claude): how many civs, you included, a new game starts with in the game's setup screens
		(Custom Game, Play Now, also Quick Start from the ini), on every map size; you can still change it there.
		0 = the map size's iDefaultPlayers (BtS: Duel 2, Tiny 3, Small 5, Standard 7, Large 9, Huge 11). The AI and the
		random events keep scaling by iDefaultPlayers (e.g. how many harbors a quest asks for). -->
	<Define>
		<DefineName>GAME_SETUP_DEFAULT_CIVS</DefineName>
		<iDefineIntVal>24</iDefineIntVal>
	</Define>
	<!-- Lake resources (written by Claude): the resources the map may place in lakes (water areas of at most 9 plots,
		LAKE_MAX_AREA_SIZE). In a lake, a listed resource needs neither its terrain nor its iMinAreaSize; its other rules
		still hold (latitude, oil not next to a river, the distance to other resources). Outside lakes nothing changes.
		Without the list no seafood goes in lakes (its iMinAreaSize is 10), and oil only on Ocean plots, while lakes are
		Coast. Bonus types from Terrain/CIV4BonusInfos.xml, separated by commas or spaces; empty = as in BtS. -->
	<Define>
		<DefineName>BONUSES_IN_LAKES</DefineName>
		<DefineTextVal>BONUS_FISH, BONUS_CRAB, BONUS_CLAM, BONUS_OIL</DefineTextVal>
	</Define>
	<!-- Options screen (written by Claude): 1 shows BtS's spare player option 1, which this mod uses for "Military Units
		Start Automated" (GameInfo/CIV4PlayerOptionInfos.xml) -->
	<Define>
		<DefineName>USE_MODDERS_PLAYEROPTION_1</DefineName>
		<iDefineIntVal>1</iDefineIntVal>
	</Define>
